proof='''Let k>=8,m>=1,rho=2^-k, g3=-1 only at000, G_m the product on m disjoint three-bit seeds, A=point_k*(1-G_m)/2, p=rho*(1-(3/4)^m)/2. Use EXACTLY stage20's one-balanced h0=u,h1=(1-A)u+A, original Qb=(Pb+delta_empty)/2, parent q-conditional lift and actual gate-conditionals with the exact mean1/2 mask. No core, gate, mask, u or padding reference is renewed. Let B=7/4-p+J/2-c1/4, old0<=U<=1/8, and retain the FULL old first-selector positive bill Tq_+<1/4. Write the averaged CURRENT complete physical signed surplus after the q query and a source-prefix as V=E_leaf(4I(F_leaf)-CE(P_leaf,Q_leaf))-U-Tq_+. The EXTRA subtraction of Tq_+ is conservative: the physical q-query change Tq is already accounted in the current leaf surplus. We never add J/2 as fresh credit.

THEOREM. Query event-source bits only. Keep padding, u, gate and mask untouched. On EACH path query at most ONE physical coordinate from each three-bit seed and at most floor(3m/4) distinct seeds. The next fresh seed and its coordinate, and stopping, may depend on the full observed history. Retain EVERY outcome and every complete reference, including constant-seed ghost coordinates without cleanup. Every adaptive tree prefix has V>5/4. This is an EXPECTED tree account, not local leaf eligibility.

PROOF. Put H0=4-9log2(3)/8. Integer3^9>2^14 gives H0<9/4 and hence 3-H0>3/4. Independent tensor spectra give H1=rho*m*H0/2+r_H, |r_H|<3. This estimate holds for ALL k>=8: the bounded entropy terms total less than2+(2k+7/2)rho<3, since k*2^-k decreases. Original core KL lies in[0,1], so c1=rho*m*H0/2+r_c with |r_c|<4. Actual edges give J=3rho*m/4+2kp. Therefore B=rho*m*(3-H0)/8+7/4+(k-1)p-r_c/4>3/4+3rho*m/32. This also certifies the original cores' rate4 eligibility. Stage20's original source identities certify full root eligibility; no arbitrary supplier is inserted.

After the q query, exact complete child costs give E(4I-CE)=B+2-p/2-phi(p)/2+[Aref(0,1/8)+Aref(p^2/4,(1+p^2)/8)]/2>=B+1-p/2, since phi<=2 and both refunds are nonnegative. These costs retain BOTH complete q terminals and the SAME original references.

At every subsequent node the full CE decrement D is a nonnegative literal frequency-marginal code charge plus average conditional-conversion KL. This is the accepted original-reference interface; both children receive the same folded ORIGINAL Q1 before their actual gate-conditional lift. Support follows from squared child coefficients<=twice folded parent squared coefficients; positive child rows inherit support. Hence total original-reach CE release L>=0 on ANY adaptive prefix.

For a fresh seed, fixing arbitrary values of every OTHER seed gives an external product sign+1 or-1. The seed-bit influence of G is1/4 at either sign. On q1 the original gate and the condition u=-1 give factor1/4; untouched padding contributesrho. Thus the CURRENT q1 fresh-seed influence is rho/16, regardless of every earlier seed outcome and of adaptive choice. Its original q1 reach1/2 makes rate4 retirement rho/8 per expected query. Uniform unqueried bits remain fair conditional on the actual history. If N is the random number of distinct queried seeds, exact physical influence conservation gives 4Pi=rho*E(N)/8<=3rho*m/32. This is a conditional expectation computation, not independence of adaptive leaves.

Consequently V>=B+1-p/2-U-Tq_+-rho*E(N)/8>3/4+1-p/2-1/8-1/4=11/8-p/2. Since p<rho/2<=1/512, V>11/8-1/1024>5/4. Every old debit, actual q-query change, complete stopped sibling and ghost remains. The original event influence is RETIRED once; no new pool is created. QED.

Dependencies rederived: eta(x)=-xlog2x, beta=(1-mu)/2,mu=(3/4)^m. The indicator entropy HB=eta(beta^2)+(mH0-eta(mu^2))/4+(1-mu^2)/2; H1=f(p)-eta(p^2)+4kp+2rho*HB, f(p)=eta((1-p)^2). Subtracting rho*mH0/2 leaves the displayed |r_H|<3. These are the independently reviewed A019 tensor identities used in stage20. Tq<1/4 and phi<=2 are stage20's proved density-only bounds, not newly assumed inherited eligibility.

Boundary audit: a second query in a previously touched seed is NOT covered. Padding queries may change the conditional event density and are NOT covered. The general negative adaptive-prefix result reported by A019 therefore is not contradicted. The first unsupported universal line is paying repeated queries within genuinely interacting/overlapping modules, or padding/source interleaving, from this SAME diminished original owner. No full FEI proof or disproof is asserted.'''
